ke, turn, grip, drift, kart, auto, surfaces, ground }): a car (the manual)\n1303:- `E.Car.collide(cars)`: bump every pair of cars that touch apart (equal weights, a little bounce)\n1306:- `car.update(dt, map, c = {})`: one step: steering, engine, grip, drift, the surface, then E.Body's walls and hop. c: an input or an intent","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016mNenWE1ceZmcf2e9wCorw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf7QpAzSQxNAy7n6ieVA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013brhdDgBwCSQogTKkNMgDi","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/x96eb17/engine/dist/handoff && sed -n 1295,1330p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-400; grep -n \"glyphs\\|settings\\.\\|menu: {\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-250 | head -40","description":"Read Car API and settings entries"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1260,"cache_read_input_tokens":109215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1260,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b632459b-63ed-4a16-8c86-b1a0aae1dd98","uuid":"b71d45f7-bf59-4a10-a7f7-2718c8bd990c","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:16:33.875Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf7QomvCudzRgQ8HBo6F","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013brhdDgBwCSQogTKkNMgDi":{"command":"cd /tmp/x96eb17/engine/dist/handoff && sed -n 1295,1330p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-400; grep -n \"glyphs\\|settings\\.\\|menu: {\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-250 | head -40","description":"Read Car API and settings entries"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013brhdDgBwCSQogTKkNMgDi","type":"tool_result","content":"- `walkbox.edges = []` †: every side of both, as [a, b]\n- `walkbox.holes` †: its holes\n- `walkbox.nodes = []` †: the corners a shortest path turns at: the outline's inward-pointing ones and every hole's outward one, set a pixel off\n- `walkbox.outline` †: the area's edge\n\n## Module drive: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it (engine/modules/drive.js)\n\n- `new E.Car(o = {}) → car`: new E.Car({ x, y, angle, top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, kart, auto, surfaces, ground }): a car (the manual)\n- `E.Car.collide(cars)`: bump every pair of cars that touch apart (equal weights, a little bounce)\n- `car.boost(sec = .8, power = .4)`: a boost: seconds of it, power (.4: top speed up by that share)\n- `car.spinOut(sec = 1)`: spin out (a shot, a hazard): seconds without control, most of its speed lost\n- `car.update(dt, map, c = {})`: one step: steering, engine, grip, drift, the surface, then E.Body's walls and hop. c: an input or an intent\n- `car.airT = 0`: a hop's seconds in the air\n- `car.angle`: its heading\n- `car.boostT = 0`: a boost's seconds left\n- `car.bumped = false`: it hit a wall or a car this step\n- `car.charge = 0`: a kart's drift boost building (1 blue, 2 orange)\n- `car.drifting = 0`: -1 left, 1 right, 0 not\n- `car.o`: its options\n- `car.offroad = false`: on a surface that slows it\n- `car.onGround = false`, `car.vz`: E.Body's (a hop leaves the ground)\n- `car.slide = 0`: sideways\n- `car.speed = 0`: along it (units a second, - backing up)\n- `car.spinT = 0`: a spin-out's\n- `car.surface = null`: the floor tag under it\n- `car.vx`, `car.vy`: its speed on the ground (E.Body's): along its heading and the slide\n- `new E.Race(o = {}) → race`: new E.Race({ path, laps, checkpoints, countdown, width, items }): a race round a closed path (the manual)\n- `race.add(car, o = {})`: a racer: its car, o.name, o.input (a player's controls) or o.ai ({ skill, rubber, lane }); returns it\n- `race.box(x, y)`: an item box at (x, y): a racer that drives through it gets an item (when it holds none)\n- `race.drive(R, dt)`: a racer's way round: the intent race.update gives an AI racer's car (look ahead along the line, bends, overtakes, unsticking, the rubber band)\n- `race.grid(n)`: the start: n places behind the line, two by two, facing along it: [{ x, y, angle }]\n- `race.hud(r, R, o = {})`: the standard HUD for a racer, in its viewport: place, lap, time, item, the countdown, WRONG WAY, FINISH (o.color; o.right: the x its right-hand text ends before, clear of a corner button)\n- `race.update(dt, map)`: one step: the countdown, every car, bumps, items, progress, laps, wrong way, places, the finish\n- `race.use(R)`: fire a racer's item: boost (now), shot (ahead along its heading), hazard (behind it)\n- `race.boxes = []`, `race.hazards = []`, `race.shots = []`: the items on the track\n- `race.go = false`: racing (the countdown over)\n261:- `game.screen.filter = 'clean'` †: 'clean' | 'scanlines' | 'crt', drawn over the picture as it is presented, never on the buffer, and not under a test harness (navigator.webdriver). game.settings.filter sets it\n266:- `game.screen.scale = 'auto'`: how a fixed resolution fills the screen: 'sharp' (whole-number scale, every pixel the same size, black bars unless o.expand grows the picture into them), 'fill' (the largest fit, pixels a device pixel apart in size\n278:- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: {\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n341:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outl\n478:- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu(\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n499:- `game.shake(a)`: shake the screen by a (pixels, decaying; at most 10 in all); none when reduceMotion, scaled by the player's settings.shake\n511:- `game.zoomBy(k)` †: the player zooms the camera by a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther), as the wheel, - and = and a pinch do (a zoom button of the game's own can): within the scene's camera.zoom range, kept as their setting (settings.zoom, \n521:- `game.drawEvery = 1`: 1, or 2 while a fast display (a 120 Hz phone) refreshes quicker than the game can draw (a frame's cost, or refreshes missed: its GPU behind): every other refresh is drawn, evenly, instead of random ones missed (the updates\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n558:- `game.zoom = 1` †: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range\n564:- `settings.default(key)`: a setting's default value\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one)\n566:- `settings.keys(group)`: the keys of a group's settings, in order ('Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Game'), or every key\n567:- `settings.reset(group)`: put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n569:- `settings.spec(key)`: the spec a setting was defined with (its label, type, range, options), or undefined\n570:- `settings.saved`: false when the last save failed (storage blocked or full: the choices last for this visit)\n576:- `fullscreen.toggle()`: full screen on or off, as the player asked (the corner's button, the menu): their choice is kept in settings.fullscreen, so a game starting on a phone goes full screen by itself only while they haven't turned it off\n1053:- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the o\n1074:- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b632459b-63ed-4a16-8c86-b1a0aae1dd98","uuid":"1e4633b3-89ad-4755-8bf8-a3fd2b715dd4","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:16:33.896Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `walkbox.edges = []` †: every side of both, as [a, b]\n- `walkbox.holes` †: its holes\n- `walkbox.nodes = []` †: the corners a shortest path turns at: the outline's inward-pointing ones and every hole's outward one, set a pixel off\n- `walkbox.outline` †: the area's edge\n\n## Module drive: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it (engine/modules/drive.js)\n\n- `new E.Car(o = {}) → car`: new E.Car({ x, y, angle, top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, kart, auto, surfaces, ground }): a car (the manual)\n- `E.Car.collide(cars)`: bump every pair of cars that touch apart (equal weights, a little bounce)\n- `car.boost(sec = .8, power = .4)`: a boost: seconds of it, power (.4: top speed up by that share)\n- `car.spinOut(sec = 1)`: spin out (a shot, a hazard): seconds without control, most of its speed lost\n- `car.update(dt, map, c = {})`: one step: steering, engine, grip, drift, the surface, then E.Body's walls and hop. c: an input or an intent\n- `car.airT = 0`: a hop's seconds in the air\n- `car.angle`: its heading\n- `car.boostT = 0`: a boost's seconds left\n- `car.bumped = false`: it hit a wall or a car this step\n- `car.charge = 0`: a kart's drift boost building (1 blue, 2 orange)\n- `car.drifting = 0`: -1 left, 1 right, 0 not\n- `car.o`: its options\n- `car.offroad = false`: on a surface that slows it\n- `car.onGround = false`, `car.vz`: E.Body's (a hop leaves the ground)\n- `car.slide = 0`: sideways\n- `car.speed = 0`: along it (units a second, - backing up)\n- `car.spinT = 0`: a spin-out's\n- `car.surface = null`: the floor tag under it\n- `car.vx`, `car.vy`: its speed on the ground (E.Body's): along its heading and the slide\n- `new E.Race(o = {}) → race`: new E.Race({ path, laps, checkpoints, countdown, width, items }): a race round a closed path (the manual)\n- `race.add(car, o = {})`: a racer: its car, o.name, o.input (a player's controls) or o.ai ({ skill, rubber, lane }); returns it\n- `race.box(x, y)`: an item box at (x, y): a racer that drives through it gets an item (when it holds none)\n- `race.drive(R, dt)`: a racer's way round: the intent race.update gives an AI racer's car (look ahead along the line, bends, overtakes, unsticking, the rubber band)\n- `race.grid(n)`: the start: n places behind the line, two by two, facing along it: [{ x, y, angle }]\n- `race.hud(r, R, o = {})`: the standard HUD for a racer, in its viewport: place, lap, time, item, the countdown, WRONG WAY, FINISH (o.color; o.right: the x its right-hand text ends before, clear of a corner button)\n- `race.update(dt, map)`: one step: the countdown, every car, bumps, items, progress, laps, wrong way, places, the finish\n- `race.use(R)`: fire a racer's item: boost (now), shot (ahead along its heading), hazard (behind it)\n- `race.boxes = []`, `race.hazards = []`, `race.shots = []`: the items on the track\n- `race.go = false`: racing (the countdown over)\n261:- `game.screen.filter = 'clean'` †: 'clean' | 'scanlines' | 'crt', drawn over the picture as it is presented, never on the buffer, and not under a test harness (navigator.webdriver). game.settings.filter sets it\n266:- `game.screen.scale = 'auto'`: how a fixed resolution fills the screen: 'sharp' (whole-number scale, every pixel the same size, black bars unless o.expand grows the picture into them), 'fill' (the largest fit, pixels a device pixel apart in size\n278:- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: {\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n341:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outl\n478:- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu(\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n499:- `game.shake(a)`: shake the screen by a (pixels, decaying; at most 10 in all); none when reduceMotion, scaled by the player's settings.shake\n511:- `game.zoomBy(k)` †: the player zooms the camera by a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther), as the wheel, - and = and a pinch do (a zoom button of the game's own can): within the scene's camera.zoom range, kept as their setting (settings.zoom, \n521:- `game.drawEvery = 1`: 1, or 2 while a fast display (a 120 Hz phone) refreshes quicker than the game can draw (a frame's cost, or refreshes missed: its GPU behind): every other refresh is drawn, evenly, instead of random ones missed (the updates\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n558:- `game.zoom = 1` †: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range\n564:- `settings.default(key)`: a setting's default value\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one)\n566:- `settings.keys(group)`: the keys of a group's settings, in order ('Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Game'), or every key\n567:- `settings.reset(group)`: put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n569:- `settings.spec(key)`: the spec a setting was defined with (its label, type, range, options), or undefined\n570:- `settings.saved`: false when the last save failed (storage blocked or full: the choices last for this visit)\n576:- `fullscreen.toggle()`: full screen on or off, as the player asked (the corner's button, the menu): their choice is kept in settings.fullscreen, so a game starting on a phone goes full screen by itself only while they haven't turned it off\n1053:- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the o\n1074:- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013brhdDgBwCSQogTKkNMgDi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
