{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UPWhVGGe1hqNhZgaFvdzRe","type":"tool_result","content":"11643 docs/ASSETS.md\n1:# Objects and materials as data\n9:## Use one\n34:## The core library\n46:## Materials on surfaces\n84:## Write one\n116:### Worked entries\n135:## Make one: the recipe\n155:## Limits\n34:## The core library\n35-\n36-**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\n37-bookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, well, sign, lamppost, anvil; fence { len: 16 }, pine { h: 41, tiers: 4 },\n38-tree { h: 40, seed: 1 }, bush { r: 7 }, grass { h: 6, n: 6 }, rock { r: 7.5, seed: 2 }, crystal { h: 18, seed: 1 }.\n39-`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.\n40-\n41-**Materials:** woods oak walnut birch crate plank planks wood; stones stone cobble marble granite sandstone slate rock\n42-brick flagstone ruin; metals iron steel gold copper bronze metal rusted; clay glazed porcelain; cloth linen burlap wool velvet leather;\n43-plants bark needles leaves shrub moss straw hedge grass; ground dirt sand snow mud; water ice crystal flame bone shingle;\n44-walls timber plaster; tops speckle plain tiles slab; tiles block bonus ground pipe checker.\n45-\n46-## Materials on surfaces\n47-\n48-```js\n49-E.MATERIALS.mossy = { color: '#6a7a5a', pattern: 'stones', size: 6 };   // or the shorthand '#6a7a5a stones size=6'\n50-const types = { 1: { h: 32, top: '#6a6280', side: '#4a4360', face: 'cobble', roof: 'slate' } };   // TileMap walls\n51-const map = new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorMat: 'flagstone', floorMats: { water: 'water' } });   // floors\n52-const level = new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types: { 1: { kind: 'solid', style: 'block', mat: 'mossy' } } });\n53-```\n54-\n55-floorMats is keyed by the floor tags of the legend ('~': { floor: 'water' }); either stands in for floorTex.\n56-\n57-A material is `{ color, pattern, ...the pattern's numbers, ramp, glow, over }`. Its five tones come from `E.tones(color)`\n58-(or its own `ramp` of five, dark to light); the light picks a band, the pattern moves it a step, so a material works on\n59-every surface and in every palette and recolors with one hex. An unknown name warns with the list of names.\n--\n138:2. **Find** the nearest entry: `node tools/asset-find.mjs \"tavern table\"` searches the core library and the store's sets\n139-   (`src/assets/sets/`, about a thousand objects, materials and sprites converted from CC0 libraries, each with where it\n140-   came from) and `--show set:id` prints one; the Asset Lab (`/asset-lab`) shows them all.\n141-3. **Copy** it and change its names, parts and materials, or write a new one from the parts above. Give the cue a player\n142-   knows it by parts of its own (a skep's coils as stacked rings, an anvil's horn, a barrow's open tub dark inside), and\n143-   keep small parts plain ('none', 'glaze'): a busy pattern on a part a few pixels wide reads as speckle.\n144-4. **Look:** `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#stool` (a file that sets `E.SHAPES.stool`, or a store set; a core id\n145-   alone works too: `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs barrel`). It draws `check-output/asset-sheet/stool.png`: every view and\n146-   four facings, beside the hero, on a light and a dark floor. It lints what reads badly: too small from above, a part\n147-   under a pixel, too few tones, low contrast with the floor, its tokens. Read the picture, fix, repeat.\n148-5. **Use** it: `E.SHAPES.stool = {...}` and `r.shape('stool', ...)`; or a set file\n149-   (`(window.ASSETS = window.ASSETS || {}).MINE = { set: 'MINE', format: 1, materials, shapes }`) and\n150-   `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS.MINE)`, which names its entries 'MINE:stool' so they never collide, and returns the names.\n151-   A store set loads the same way (its script, then `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`);\n152-   `node tools/asset-set.mjs <sets> --ids a,b --name mine --out mine.js` cuts the few a game uses, with what they need\n153-   (Emberdeep's set dressing loads `src/assets/sets/emberdeep.js`, cut so).\n154-\n155-## Limits\n156-\n157-- Still objects. Lids that open, swinging signs and held weapons are code (or props) for now.\n158-- A shape sorts by one point, as props do; a long one (a bed, a cart) may cross a body walking right beside it.\n159-- Collision is the footprint's box, turned with the shape, and the bounds' height: a table is solid under its top too.\n160-- Bigger than about 240 pixels on screen, a shape skips the actors' effects (flash, x-ray).\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b632459b-63ed-4a16-8c86-b1a0aae1dd98","uuid":"d76c5bed-4ed7-4ed4-b171-b76d7174d003","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:18:20.571Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"11643 docs/ASSETS.md\n1:# Objects and materials as data\n9:## Use one\n34:## The core library\n46:## Materials on surfaces\n84:## Write one\n116:### Worked entries\n135:## Make one: the recipe\n155:## Limits\n34:## The core library\n35-\n36-**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\n37-bookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, well, sign, lamppost, anvil; fence { len: 16 }, pine { h: 41, tiers: 4 },\n38-tree { h: 40, seed: 1 }, bush { r: 7 }, grass { h: 6, n: 6 }, rock { r: 7.5, seed: 2 }, crystal { h: 18, seed: 1 }.\n39-`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.\n40-\n41-**Materials:** woods oak walnut birch crate plank planks wood; stones stone cobble marble granite sandstone slate rock\n42-brick flagstone ruin; metals iron steel gold copper bronze metal rusted; clay glazed porcelain; cloth linen burlap wool velvet leather;\n43-plants bark needles leaves shrub moss straw hedge grass; ground dirt sand snow mud; water ice crystal flame bone shingle;\n44-walls timber plaster; tops speckle plain tiles slab; tiles block bonus ground pipe checker.\n45-\n46-## Materials on surfaces\n47-\n48-```js\n49-E.MATERIALS.mossy = { color: '#6a7a5a', pattern: 'stones', size: 6 };   // or the shorthand '#6a7a5a stones size=6'\n50-const types = { 1: { h: 32, top: '#6a6280', side: '#4a4360', face: 'cobble', roof: 'slate' } };   // TileMap walls\n51-const map = new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorMat: 'flagstone', floorMats: { water: 'water' } });   // floors\n52-const level = new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types: { 1: { kind: 'solid', style: 'block', mat: 'mossy' } } });\n53-```\n54-\n55-floorMats is keyed by the floor tags of the legend ('~': { floor: 'water' }); either stands in for floorTex.\n56-\n57-A material is `{ color, pattern, ...the pattern's numbers, ramp, glow, over }`. Its five tones come from `E.tones(color)`\n58-(or its own `ramp` of five, dark to light); the light picks a band, the pattern moves it a step, so a material works on\n59-every surface and in every palette and recolors with one hex. An unknown name warns with the list of names.\n--\n138:2. **Find** the nearest entry: `node tools/asset-find.mjs \"tavern table\"` searches the core library and the store's sets\n139-   (`src/assets/sets/`, about a thousand objects, materials and sprites converted from CC0 libraries, each with where it\n140-   came from) and `--show set:id` prints one; the Asset Lab (`/asset-lab`) shows them all.\n141-3. **Copy** it and change its names, parts and materials, or write a new one from the parts above. Give the cue a player\n142-   knows it by parts of its own (a skep's coils as stacked rings, an anvil's horn, a barrow's open tub dark inside), and\n143-   keep small parts plain ('none', 'glaze'): a busy pattern on a part a few pixels wide reads as speckle.\n144-4. **Look:** `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#stool` (a file that sets `E.SHAPES.stool`, or a store set; a core id\n145-   alone works too: `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs barrel`). It draws `check-output/asset-sheet/stool.png`: every view and\n146-   four facings, beside the hero, on a light and a dark floor. It lints what reads badly: too small from above, a part\n147-   under a pixel, too few tones, low contrast with the floor, its tokens. Read the picture, fix, repeat.\n148-5. **Use** it: `E.SHAPES.stool = {...}` and `r.shape('stool', ...)`; or a set file\n149-   (`(window.ASSETS = window.ASSETS || {}).MINE = { set: 'MINE', format: 1, materials, shapes }`) and\n150-   `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS.MINE)`, which names its entries 'MINE:stool' so they never collide, and returns the names.\n151-   A store set loads the same way (its script, then `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`);\n152-   `node tools/asset-set.mjs <sets> --ids a,b --name mine --out mine.js` cuts the few a game uses, with what they need\n153-   (Emberdeep's set dressing loads `src/assets/sets/emberdeep.js`, cut so).\n154-\n155-## Limits\n156-\n157-- Still objects. Lids that open, swinging signs and held weapons are code (or props) for now.\n158-- A shape sorts by one point, as props do; a long one (a bed, a cart) may cross a body walking right beside it.\n159-- Collision is the footprint's box, turned with the shape, and the bounds' height: a table is solid under its top too.\n160-- Bigger than about 240 pixels on screen, a shape skips the actors' effects (flash, x-ray).","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UPWhVGGe1hqNhZgaFvdzRe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
