hesized sound effects (typewriter, phone, ice, projector, applause) and Simlish gibberish voices pitched per character',\\n    'Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode (1-4 players; seeded deal, position sharing, progress and results); no other network use',\\n    'Testing: headless Chromium via Playwright (engine check tool, scripted play-throughs), the AI Hub harness in automatic mode; WebKit and Firefox screenshots via viewport-matrix; no real phones or real iOS Safari',\\n    'Research: none online beyond the engine and hub documentation; the source was drawn from general knowledge of the series',\\n    'Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown',\\n    'Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium',\\n    'Usage: unknown']],\\n  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\\n    'Issues caught by testing: see the chat reply and exit-interview.json of this build.',\\n    'Most helpful test: a scripted headless play-through of a whole day (office, brainstorm, pitch, verdict).',\\n    'Least helpful: full-screen screenshots of static title screens.']],\\n  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', [\\n    'Liked most: shapes as data, the dialog box with live portraits, and coroutine scripts on game time.',\\n    'Built myself: the pitch card battle, the delivery and closer meters, controller glyph icons, the attract-mode bot.',\\n    'Hardest: the pixel font has no PlayStation shape glyphs, so prompts needed hand-drawn buttons.']],\\n  ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', ['Liked: the freedom to pick the genre. Hardest: fitting attract mode, local versus and AI Hub into one vertical slice.']],\\n  ['CREDITS', ['Design, writing, code, music and sound: Claude (Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5) for the cc-matrix run.', 'Engine: my-3D2dge by Michael Crosato. Session client: AI Hub.', 'Thanks to the Sterling Cooper of our imaginations. No accounts were harmed.']]\\n];\\n})();\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[],\"originalFile\":null,\"userModified\":false},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_014XkA