nd the four sections are in my previous message in full. A search of the source found no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\\n\\nWhat remains is outside what I can verify here: a real controller, real iOS Safari, and listening to the voices. The 13-viewport matrix only captured the title screen; gameplay ran at five sizes with no JS errors. The title was picked over a list the code checked at exactly 50 distinct titles, and the first 51-entry list was discarded.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":853,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":310043,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":853,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":325,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c2ae8259-5c55-47b1-bacf-f99cf4152c08\",\"uuid\":\"4ed0e51a-b9ac-4f83-a970-126d3e6796ff\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T01:40:46.367Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgf9Fcu4Gt2g9TEckv2Ep\"}"," {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Stop hook feedback:\\n[Read TASK.md in the current folder and complete the task it describes. Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The stop condition's 'done when' terms are not fully evidenced. The bundled HTML and exit-interview.json exist, and the four sections appear in the earlier assistant message, but the final message does not contain them and points back instead. The last message also states the 13-viewport matrix 'only captured the title screen', the voices were never heard ('I still have not heard it'), and the 50-title requirement was met by a re-pick after a 51-entry list was discarded. TASK.md requires every feature to be implemented and verified, which the transcript does not show.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c2ae8259-5c55-47b1-bacf-f99cf4152c08\",\"uuid\":\"bdf861c6-1767-4c95-928e-8751c8bd8011\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T01:40:48.298Z\",\"isSynthetic\":true}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgf9GCcLoiB6rXhSonrJf\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Here are the four sections in this message, so the reply stands alone. The first section is Source Information.\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-02 18:13\\n- **Source:** The Wire (2002-2008), kept as gritty and real as the show. Characters and places are original.\\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Investigation / stealth / action-adventure. Three-quarter top-down camera; V or R3 switches to top-down or isometric.\\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.1 handoff (engine, TileMap, Mover, Humanoid rigs, Suspicion, Dialog, Menu, Bullets, FlowField, canvas lighting). AI Hub session client 1.3.0. Plain JavaScript, no other libraries.\\n- **Art Direction:** Engine-native pixel art at 320x240, expanded to any screen. Shaded character rigs, brick blocks, rain, streetlamp and flashlight lighting.\\n- **Animation:** Engine-native procedural character rigs with poses, expressions and live dialog portraits. Particles and hit effects.\\n- **Audio:** All written in code: six music loops, synth sound effects, and Animalese-style gibberish voices (one note per typed letter, pitched per speaker).\\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel mode, 1–4 players. Nothing else on the network.\\n- **Testing:** Headless Chromium and WebKit via Playwright:\\n  - the attract-mode AI playing the full case;\\n  - keyboard tests of photos, tip, tap, wire logging and the raid;\\n  - a mocked DualSense for axis inversion and glyphs;\\n  - touch emulation;\\n  - the 13-viewport matrix (title screen only);\\n  - a five-size gameplay pass;\\n  - the hub harness;\\n  - a check that voice notes vary by letter.\\n  \\n  No real controller or real iOS Safari.\\n- **Research:** Read the engine card, the stealth and adventure kits and the hub protocol. No web research on the show.\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- **Usage:** unknown\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n- **Issues caught:** About 9. An unreachable room (a table blocked a doorway), attract mode stalling on dialog, symbols the font can't draw (several), cuff range lost after a shove, an enemy facing away with no gun, a menu hiding the title cast, a tagline cut off on phones, and a stale test server.\\n- **Critical:** 2. The blocked doorway made the raid unfinishable, and the demo froze on the judge's dialog.\\n- **Most helpful test:** The attract-mode run. The demo plays the whole case, so one scripted pass hit every scene and found both critical bugs.\\n- **Least helpful test:** The viewport-matrix screenshots. Only the title screen was reachable there, so they showed layout but few bugs.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** Humanoid rigs with live dialog portraits, and the free pause, settings, controls and glyph options. Mover, sees and Suspicion gave stealth almost for free.\\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Yes. I guessed the font had pad symbols (it doesn't), that `game.go` switches at once (it fades first), and that `input.tap` counts as keyboard (it flips prompts to touch).\\n- **Built myself:** The wire-room listening game, the case board, raid combat, the attract-mode driver, pixel-drawn pad symbols, and a gamepad axis-inversion shim.\\n- **Hardest part:** Building screens that aren't the game world. The canvas UI kit is thin for text-heavy or card screens, and FlowField treats any tall prop as a wall.\\n- **Remove or overhaul:** The split between the canvas Menu and the HTML settings screens. One UI system would be simpler.\\n- **Change one thing:** Add built-in gamepad axis inversion and a font that includes controller face-button symbols.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** Clear deliverables, the controller-first rules, and the exit-interview JSON that tools read.\\n- **Confusing:** Whether the source name includes the phrase after the dash, and how Online and Multiplayer differ.\\n- **Hardest:** Scope. A feature-complete slice with attract mode, hub play and a 10-foot UI, tested only in headless browsers.\\n- **One test I'd have run:** Play the whole game start to finish with a real DualSense on a TV.\\n\\n## Still unverified\\n- **Voices:** I checked that the voice code varies notes by letter, not the sound. I never heard it, because the headless browser has no sound.\\n- **Real hardware:** I never ran a real controller or real iOS Safari.\\n- **Viewports:** the 13-viewport matrix only captured the title screen. Gameplay ran at five sizes with no JS errors.\\n- **Title list:** the game is **Fifty Percent Chance of Probable Cause**, picked over a list the code checked at 50 distinct titles. My first list had 51 entries and was discarded.\\n- **AI Hub harness:** it reported PASS for 2 players on the current build.\\n\\nThe bundle is `Fifty Percent Chance of Probable Cause-The Wire (2002-2008) - Keep it as gritty and real as the show-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-181334.html` in the folder root. `exit-interview.json` sits beside it and parses with every field filled. A search of the source found no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":649,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":310896,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":649,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c2ae8259-5c55-47b1-bacf-f99cf4152c08\",\"uuid\":\"5fd79a74-7966-4e04-9ade-44e079df148d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T01:41:00.464Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgf9GC94R9jtJtQbYGNBY\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181340__x96eb17/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":732,"oldLines":3,"newStart":732,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgf9D7WR7bLftbd6UG5Li\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_0115APuVefgefZonwTxJL3nh\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"until [ -f /tmp/sdtest/w_18.png ] || ! pgrep -f \\\"[t]5.py\\\" >/dev/null; do sleep 3; done; cut -c1-170 /tmp/sdtest/t5.log\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1509,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":254112,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1509,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":6,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f9b39171-d84f-4593-93cb-80dd0e6441b3\",\"uuid\":\"2e90bacd-7af8-427c-add0-cdbc3856dc63\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T01:40:09.387Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgf9D6j3uu5vdc1dNj9nw\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_0115APuVefgefZonwTxJL3nh\":{\"command\":\"until [ -f /tmp/sdtest/w_18.png ] || ! pgrep -f \\\"[t]5.py\\\" >/dev/null; do sleep 3; done; cut -c1-170 /tmp/sdtest/t5.log\"}}}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_started\