stomp) and touch-only attract mode on an iPhone profile (all pass); ghosts received on every copy in a live hub round; AI Hub harness with 2 players\\\")\\nopen('record.mjs','w').write(s)\\nEOF\\ngrep -c \\\"15 issues\\\" record.mjs; cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316 && node /tmp/x96eb17/gen.mjs src/about.js ../exit-interview.json && node build.mjs && node test.mjs | tail -1 && python3 -c \\\"import json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print('json ok', d['testingFeedback'][0][:10])\\\"\",\"description\":\"Update record, regenerate About and exit interview, rebuild, retest\",\"timeout\":200000}}}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_started\",\"task_id\":\"b61rr01jn\",\"run_id\":\"0mw01gfwx-be84a87c\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01WN7GaVon4A3ZCJxTVULD5n\",\"description\":\"Update record, regenerate About and exit interview, rebuild, retest\",\"is_backgrounded\":false,\"task_type\":\"local_bash\",\"uuid\":\"dae11287-f0a9-4904-8f53-d43eb3c5b1fe\",\"session_id\":\"b632459b-63ed-4a16-8c86-b1a0aae1dd98\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_notification\",\"task_id\":\"b61rr01jn\",\"run_id\":\"0mw01gfwx-be84a87c\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01WN7GaVon4A3ZCJxTVULD5n\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"output_file\":\"\",\"summary\":\"Update record, regenerate About and exit interview, rebuild, retest\",\"uuid\":\"7b4ef5d6-069f-47de-b05c-1480abd64c9a\",\"session_id\":\"b632459b-63ed-4a16-8c86-b1a0aae1dd98\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316.html","hunks":[{"oldStart":15228,"oldLines":7,"newStart":15228,"newLines":7,"lines":["    \"# Online\",","    \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players: a timed Collection Run on every copy with the other players shown as translucent ghosts, progress and result reporting. On its own: local 2-player drop-in co-op (player 2 is Chrissy), no network\",","    \"# Testing\",","-   \"Headless Node test of the whole story and the Collection Run (fixed-step game.advance, scripted input; all checks pass); Playwright screenshots in Chromium 1280x720 and WebKit iPhone 15 (touch-only screen, attract mode); viewport-matrix on 23 phone, tablet and desktop viewports in Chromium, WebKit and Firefox (all clean); AI Hub harness with 2 players, 4 players at 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss, and host-leave (all PASS). No real gamepad, TV or iOS Safari\",","+   \"Headless Node test of the whole story and the Collection Run (fixed-step game.advance, scripted input; all checks pass); Playwright screenshots in Chromium 1280x720 and WebKit iPhone 15 (touch-only screen, attract mode); viewport-matrix on 23 phone, tablet and desktop viewports in Chromium, WebKit and Firefox (all clean); a feature check with an emulated DualSense (stick movement, both invert toggles, PlayStation and Xbox symbols, prompts switching to keys and mouse buttons, the stomp) and touch-only attract mode on an iPhone profile (all pass); ghosts received on every copy in a live hub round; AI Hub harness with 2 players, 4 players at 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss, and host-leave (all PASS). No real gamepad, TV or iOS Safari\",","    \"# Research\",","    \"None on the web. I read the engine's handoff docs (README, API card, parts of the index, the template and the brawler kit) and the AI Hub protocol README; the show's details come from memory\",","    \"# Environment\","]},{"oldStart":15243,"oldLines":7,"newStart":15243,"newLines":7,"lines":["   \"title\": \"TESTING\",","   \"lines\": [","    \"# How many issues did testing catch?\",","-   \"14 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space.\",","+   \"14 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space. Hovering the mouse never counted as using the mouse, because the engine only switches to the mouse on a click, so hover focus and mouse-button prompts didn't work until a click.\",","    \"# How many were critical / game breaking?\",","    \"4 were critical or game-breaking. The title crash broke attract mode. The fight waves never advancing blocked chapter 4. The missing booth step blocked the finale. The finale leaking into the Collection Run ended runs early.\",","    \"# Most helpful test\","]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316/index.html","hunks":[{"oldStart":15228,"oldLines":7,"newStart":15228,"newLines":7,"lines":["    \"# Online\",","    \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players: a timed Collection Run on every copy with the other players shown as translucent ghosts, progress and result reporting. On its own: local 2-player drop-in co-op (player 2 is Chrissy), no network\",","    \"# Testing\",","-   \"Headless Node test of the whole story and the Collection Run (fixed-step game.advance, scripted input; all checks pass); Playwright screenshots in Chromium 1280x720 and WebKit iPhone 15 (touch-only screen, attract mode); viewport-matrix on 23 phone, tablet and desktop viewports in Chromium, WebKit and Firefox (all clean); AI Hub harness with 2 players, 4 players at 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss, and host-leave (all PASS). No real gamepad, TV or iOS Safari\",","+   \"Headless Node test of the whole story and the Collection Run (fixed-step game.advance, scripted input; all checks pass); Playwright screenshots in Chromium 1280x720 and WebKit iPhone 15 (touch-only screen, attract mode); viewport-matrix on 23 phone, tablet and desktop viewports in Chromium, WebKit and Firefox (all clean); a feature check with an emulated DualSense (stick movement, both invert toggles, PlayStation and Xbox symbols, prompts switching to keys and mouse buttons, the stomp) and touch-only attract mode on an iPhone profile (all pass); ghosts received on every copy in a live hub round; AI Hub harness with 2 players, 4 players at 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss, and host-leave (all PASS). No real gamepad, TV or iOS Safari\",","    \"# Research\",","    \"None on the web. I read the engine's handoff docs (README, API card, parts of the index, the template and the brawler kit) and the AI Hub protocol README; the show's details come from memory\",","    \"# Environment\","]},{"oldStart":15243,"oldLines":7,"newStart":15243,"newLines":7,"lines":["   \"title\": \"TESTING\",","   \"lines\": [","    \"# How many issues did testing catch?\",","-   \"14 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space.\",","+   \"14 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space. Hovering the mouse never counted as using the mouse, because the engine only switches to the mouse on a click, so hover focus and mouse-button prompts didn't work until a click.\",","    \"# How many were critical / game breaking?\",","    \"4 were critical or game-breaking. The title crash broke attract mode. The fight waves never advancing blocked chapter 4. The missing booth step blocked the finale. The finale leaking into the Collection Run ended runs early.\",","    \"# Most helpful test\","]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316/src/about.js","hunks":[{"oldStart":21,"oldLines":7,"newStart":21,"newLines":7,"lines":["    \"# Online\",","    \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players: a timed Collection Run on every copy with the other players shown as translucent ghosts, progress and result reporting. On its own: local 2-player drop-in co-op (player 2 is Chrissy), no network\",","    \"# Testing\",","-   \"Headless Node test of the whole story and the Collection Run (fixed-step game.advance, scripted input; all checks pass); Playwright screenshots in Chromium 1280x720 and WebKit iPhone 15 (touch-only screen, attract mode); viewport-matrix on 23 phone, tablet and desktop viewports in Chromium, WebKit and Firefox (all clean); AI Hub harness with 2 players, 4 players at 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss, and host-leave (all PASS). No real gamepad, TV or iOS Safari\",","+   \"Headless Node test of the whole story and the Collection Run (fixed-step game.advance, scripted input; all checks pass); Playwright screenshots in Chromium 1280x720 and WebKit iPhone 15 (touch-only screen, attract mode); viewport-matrix on 23 phone, tablet and desktop viewports in Chromium, WebKit and Firefox (all clean); a feature check with an emulated DualSense (stick movement, both invert toggles, PlayStation and Xbox symbols, prompts switching to keys and mouse buttons, the stomp) and touch-only attract mode on an iPhone profile (all pass); ghosts received on every copy in a live hub round; AI Hub harness with 2 players, 4 players at 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss, and host-leave (all PASS). No real gamepad, TV or iOS Safari\",","    \"# Research\",","    \"None on the web. I read the engine's handoff docs (README, API card, parts of the index, the template and the brawler kit) and the AI Hub protocol README; the show's details come from memory\",","    \"# Environment\","]},{"oldStart":36,"oldLines":7,"newStart":36,"newLines":7,"lines":["   \"title\": \"TESTING\",","   \"lines\": [","    \"# How many issues did testing catch?\",","-   \"14 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space.\",","+   \"14 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space. Hovering the mouse never counted as using the mouse, because the engine only switches to the mouse on a click, so hover focus and mouse-button prompts didn't work until a click.\",","    \"# How many were critical / game breaking?\",","    \"4 were critical or game-breaking. The title crash broke attract mode. The fight waves never advancing blocked chapter 4. The missing booth step blocked the finale. The finale leaking into the Collection Run ended runs early.\",","    \"# Most helpful test\","]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/exit-interview.json","hunks":[{"oldStart":9,"oldLines":14,"newStart":9,"newLines":14,"lines":["     \"animation\": \"Engine-native skeletal Humanoid rigs posed from velocity every step, E.MOVES attacks (jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, plunge stomp, roundhouse, bash, elbow), knock-downs and get-ups, Blob ducks and a pig, scripted cutscenes (game.script), tweens and particles\",","     \"audio\": \"Code-written chip music (11 original tracker songs, including 3 jukebox songs the player picks), synthesized sound effects (punches, gunshots, horn, quacks, diner bell, cash), and Animalese-style gibberish voices with a pitch and timbre per character\",","     \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players: a timed Collection Run on every copy with the other players shown as translucent ghosts, progress and result reporting. On its own: local 2-player drop-in co-op (player 2 is Chrissy), no network\",","-    \"testing\": \"Headless Node test of the whole story and the Collection Run (fixed-step game.advance, scripted input; all checks pass); Playwright screenshots in Chromium 1280x720 and WebKit iPhone 15 (touch-only screen, attract mode); viewport-matrix on 23 phone, tablet and desktop viewports in Chromium, WebKit and Firefox (all clean); AI Hub harness with 2 players, 4 players at 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss, and host-leave (all PASS). No real gamepad, TV or iOS Safari\",","+    \"testing\": \"Headless Node test of the whole story and the Collection Run (fixed-step game.advance, scripted input; all checks pass); Playwright screenshots in Chromium 1280x720 and WebKit iPhone 15 (touch-only screen, attract mode); viewport-matrix on 23 phone, tablet and desktop viewports in Chromium, WebKit and Firefox (all clean); a feature check with an emulated DualSense (stick movement, both invert toggles, PlayStation and Xbox symbols, prompts switching to keys and mouse buttons, the stomp) and touch-only attract mode on an iPhone profile (all pass); ghosts received on every copy in a live hub round; AI Hub harness with 2 players, 4 players at 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss, and host-leave (all PASS). No real gamepad, TV or iOS Safari\",","     \"research\": \"None on the web. I read the engine's handoff docs (README, API card, parts of the index, the template and the brawler kit) and the AI Hub protocol README; the show's details come from memory\",","     \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",","     \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",","     \"usage\": \"Cost and token totals are unknown: this session has no usage meter. Session time was about 40 minutes (18:13 to 18:53)\"","   },","   \"testingFeedback\": [","-    \"14 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space.\",","+    \"14 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space. Hovering the mouse never counted as using the mouse, because the engine only switches to the mouse on a click, so hover focus and mouse-button prompts didn't work until a click.\",","     \"4 were critical or game-breaking. The title crash broke attract mode. The fight waves never advancing blocked chapter 4. The missing booth step blocked the finale. The finale leaking into the Collection Run ended runs early.\",","     \"The headless Node test (test.mjs). It plays the whole story through game.debug: the paper, ducks, the car, therapy, breathing, the pork store, three collections, the alley fight, Ma, the yard waves, Ralphie, the diner, the cut to black, then the Collection Run. It caught every blocking bug in seconds.\",","     \"Setting the stress straight to 100 for a panic screenshot. That skips addStress(), so no panic attack ever started and the picture only showed the RAGE bar.\""]}]}],"moreFiles":5,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316.html","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316/index.html","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316/src/about.js","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/exit-interview.json","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181319__xb81546/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181337__x3ec78e/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184349__x8b64cc/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-185709__x694301/agent.out"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WN7GaVon4A3ZCJxTVULD5n","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
