{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfB678tWvYAfp2T3v1z3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The feedback asked for visible proof rather than counters. Here is what I could show on screen; real hardware is the one thing I couldn't check.\n\n**Shown on screen:**\n- **Controller prompts:** with an emulated DualSense, the HUD draws Xbox buttons when that setting is on (X Punch, Y Haymaker, B Roll, RT Pistol, LT Breathe). Earlier screenshots show the PlayStation shapes. Movement and both invert toggles were checked with the same emulated pad.\n- **Mouse hover:** standing near the SUV, the prompt said \"Get in the SUV\". Pointing the mouse at the pork store door switched it to the door, and clicking went inside. Making that work found two things I fixed:\n  - **A bug:** hovering never counted as using the mouse until you clicked, so hover focus and mouse-button prompts didn't work.\n  - **A tweak:** the mouse can now pick things up to 64 units away instead of 40.\n- **Attract mode on touch-only devices:** on both an Android (Pixel 7, Chromium) and an iPhone (WebKit) profile, the title shows \"Controller or keyboard required\", the demo starts on its own after 10 seconds, and a tap returns to the title.\n- **Ghosts in a live hub round:** each player sees the other on screen as a tinted ghost with their name and cash (\"Blue Otter $0\" on Red Fox's screen, \"Red Fox $0\" on Blue Otter's).\n\n**Not checkable here:**\n- **Real hardware:** no physical DualSense, TV or iOS Safari is available, so those stay untested.\n- **Usage:** cost and token counts are \"unknown\" because this session has no usage meter. TASK.md asks for \"unknown\" when something can't be confirmed.\n\nOn the final bundle the headless story test passes, and the 4-player lossy-network hub harness reports PASS. `exit-interview.json` parses and still answers every field. Its testing answers, and the in-game About page, were written before this round: they don't list the hover change or these newest checks, and the session time is still 18:13–18:53.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-02 18:13\n- **Source:** The Sopranos (HBO, 1999-2007), created by David Chase\n- **Genre and Perspective:** an action-adventure crime brawler in a small open town (story chapters, melee and a pistol, driving, dialogue choices, stress/panic, FBI heat). Three-quarter top-down by default, switchable to isometric or top-down (V / R3).\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (full engine, single file); AI Hub session client 1.3.0 (Protocol v1); vanilla JavaScript, canvas 2D, Web Audio; bundled with Node 24; tested with Playwright 1.63\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native code-drawn pixel art at PS1 resolution, expanded to fill the screen. Dressed HD Humanoid rigs, textured walls and floors, props, lighting, rain and neon, plus custom-drawn cars and furniture.\n- **Animation:** the engine's skeletal Humanoid rigs with its built-in attack moves, knock-downs and get-ups; Blob ducks and a pig; scripted cutscenes, tweens and particles.\n- **Audio:** 11 original code-written songs (three are jukebox picks), synthesized sound effects, and gibberish voices pitched per character.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players (Collection Run, ghosts, progress and result reporting). On its own, the game has local 2-player co-op and no network.\n- **Testing:**\n  - headless Node test of the full story plus the Collection Run (all checks pass)\n  - Chromium and WebKit screenshots\n  - viewport-matrix: 23 viewports clean\n  - emulated-DualSense checks: stick movement, both invert toggles, PlayStation and Xbox prompts\n  - prompts switching to keys and mouse buttons; mouse hover and click in the world\n  - touch-only attract mode on Chromium and WebKit phone profiles\n  - ghosts visible on every copy in a live hub round\n  - AI Hub harness: PASS with 2 players, with 4 players at 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss, and with the host leaving\n  - nothing tested on a real gamepad, TV or iOS Safari\n- **Research:** none on the web. I read the engine's handoff docs and the AI Hub README; details of the show come from memory.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown (no usage meter in this session). The first finished build took about 40 minutes (18:13–18:53), the figure in the exit interview and About page; with the follow-up checks the session ran to about 19:00.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** 15, plus one more found after the exit interview was written (the mouse reach was too short at 40 units):\n  - the title screen crashed when the town updated with no hero\n  - fight waves never advanced\n  - the diner booth step was never set\n  - a pending fight was lost on a scene change\n  - attract mode left the camera in isometric view\n  - the finale's state leaked into the Collection Run\n  - Tony couldn't get out of the SUV while it was reversing\n  - the touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device\n  - the touch-only notice overflowed its box on narrow phones\n  - talk prompts appeared during fights\n  - job log text overlapped its Close prompt\n  - the attract mode's title covered the HUD\n  - the SUV prompt radius was too small\n  - gamepad right-stick aim wasn't converted from screen to world direction\n  - hovering the mouse didn't count as using the mouse until a click\n- **How many were critical?** 4: the title crash (it broke attract mode), the stuck fight waves (they blocked chapter 4), the missing booth step (it blocked the finale), and the finale leaking into the Collection Run.\n- **Most helpful test:** the headless Node playthrough of the whole story through the game's debug handle. It found every blocking bug within seconds.\n- **Least helpful test:** setting stress straight to 100 for a panic-attack screenshot. That bypasses the code that starts a panic, so nothing happened.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the standard features I didn't have to build (pause, settings, rebinding, controller symbols, saves, boot screen), the Humanoid rigs with their attack moves, and fixed-step headless testing.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong?** Yes:\n  - the pixel font lacks a check mark, a middle dot and a down triangle\n  - the \"last device\" starts as keyboard, and only switches to mouse on a click\n  - scripts can't wait on promises\n  - braking the car turns into reversing\n  - `game.after` timers are cleared on a scene change\n- **Most important thing I built:** a renderer for rotated 3D boxes, which draws the cars and furniture correctly in every camera view. Close behind: the controller and keyboard prompt badges, since the font has no button symbols.\n- **Hardest part:** the volume of documentation (a 190 KB API index), and finding which props and options exist.\n- **Remove or overhaul:** dialogue voices. One sound per dialog box can't give each speaker their own gibberish voice, so I wrote my own.\n- **Change one thing:** built-in canvas prompt glyphs for each controller family, and a \"has a keyboard, mouse or pad\" flag.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** a clear checklist of required systems with open creative design, and an exit interview that makes the result easy to audit.\n- **Confusing:** whether the game on its own should be online or whether local co-op is enough (I chose local co-op). Also, how to write a title with spaces in the file name.\n- **Hardest:** the scope (a five-chapter slice with combat, driving, heat, stress, saves, attract mode and hub ghost mode), and writing dialogue that sounds like the show without copying it.\n- **The one test I'd have run:** a real DualSense on a TV at 10 feet, including a pad that reports its axes inverted. Real iOS Safari would be next."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":375122,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":338,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":737,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b632459b-63ed-4a16-8c86-b1a0aae1dd98","uuid":"3d1859dd-2176-4b8f-bc51-cd1fd767f536","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:05:06.595Z","request_id":"req_011CgfB66fcReZP7jM4ajeCs"}
