{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfBXgGdnuBsR2RFRy4ZG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Same verdict and same blocker. I'm waiting on you for one of these:\n- **Press a button on the Luna controller** with the game open in Edge or Chrome on Windows, then check the prompts and the invert toggles yourself.\n- **Approve installing ViGEmBus**, a virtual-controller driver, and I'll drive the test in Edge myself.\n- **Run `/goal clear`** to accept the emulated checks as they stand.\n\nThe game, `exit-interview.json`, and the four sections from my earlier replies (Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback) are unchanged and complete.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-02 18:13\n- **Source:** The Sopranos (HBO, 1999-2007), created by David Chase\n- **Genre and Perspective:** action-adventure crime brawler; three-quarter top-down, switchable to isometric and top-down\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.1; AI Hub session client 1.3.0; JavaScript, canvas 2D, Web Audio\n- **Art Direction:** engine-native code-drawn pixel art at PS1 resolution\n- **Animation:** engine skeletal Humanoid rigs and built-in attack moves, scripted cutscenes\n- **Audio:** code-written music and sound effects, gibberish voices\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players; local co-op on its own\n- **Testing:**\n  - headless story test\n  - 23 viewports clean\n  - emulated-DualSense checks\n  - AI Hub harness PASS\n  - no real controller test (needs a person to press a button), no TV or iOS Safari\n- **Research:** none on the web\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown. `exit-interview.json` says about 50 minutes, which doesn't include the Windows controller check that came after.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** 16\n- **Critical:** 4\n- **Most helpful test:** the headless story playthrough\n- **Least helpful test:** the stress-to-100 screenshot\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the standard features it gives you for free, the rigs, and headless testing\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong?** Yes: font glyphs, the last-device default, script promises, car braking, timers\n- **Most important thing I built:** the renderer for rotated 3D boxes\n- **Hardest part:** the volume of documentation\n- **Remove or overhaul:** dialogue voices\n- **Change one thing:** built-in controller glyphs\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the clear checklist of required systems\n- **Confusing:** whether the game should be online on its own, and file naming\n- **Hardest:** the scope\n- **The one test I'd have run:** a real DualSense on a TV"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1784,"cache_read_input_tokens":415400,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1784,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b632459b-63ed-4a16-8c86-b1a0aae1dd98","uuid":"ea7b39a3-94b0-415a-a9eb-f44d6c8e5ac0","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:10:40.535Z","request_id":"req_011CgfBXftKyshhSvHrPiQdY"}
